<title>UK: UK watchdog started probing Sumitomo in January.</title>
<headline>UK watchdog started probing Sumitomo in January.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Investments Board (SIB) launched an inquiry into the copper trading activities of Sumitomo Corp of Japan as early as January, SIB Chief Executive Andrew Winckler said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Winckler told parliament's Treasury Select Committee that the SIB had contacted the U.S. Commodities Futures Trading Commission (CFTC) about the world copper market even earlier and was now cooperating extremely closely with it on the probe.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm happy, if this helps the committee, to say ...though we would not normally ever reveal these things, that we began that inquiry in January of this year,&quot; Winckler told the committee.</p>
</text>
